        "id": "ev-member",
        "kind": "code",
        "locator": {
          "lineRange": {
            "end": 15,
            "start": 1
          },
          "path": "members/models.py",
          "symbol": "Member"
        },
        "summary": "Member is declared as a subclass of Django's AbstractUser and adds membership_number, is_librarian and joined_on; display derives a name."
      },
      {
        "contentDigest": "sha256:f6fd76d8d7f0994014f95a0fdaee3ce021b70741e004a99c6cc4fc11b1886b37",
        "id": "ev-auth-user-model",
        "kind": "configuration",
        "locator": {
          "lineRange": {
            "end": 56,
            "start": 56
          },
          "path": "shelfmark/settings.py",
          "symbol": "AUTH_USER_MODEL"
        },
        "summary": "AUTH_USER_MODEL is members.Member, so every settings.AUTH_USER_MODEL foreign key in the project points at Member."
      },
      {
        "contentDigest": "sha256:f24e90bf66420e63b66be4f9948a4c93c8c7d7fed96e3cd3aadf8a696c05d94f",
        "id": "ev-book",
        "kind": "code",
        "locator": {
          "lineRange": {
            "end": 22,
            "start": 4
          },
          "path": "catalog/models.py",
          "symbol": "Book"
        },
        "summary": "Book stores title, author, a unique isbn, published_year, replacement_cost_minor and high_demand; copies_available is computed from its copies."
      },
      {
        "contentDigest": "sha256:b73f9735b5053749ff8cd0d5db22aa42c135eef8e37a3532d65a04d9a8c6c42f",
        "id": "ev-copy",
        "kind": "code",
        "locator": {
          "lineRange": {
            "end": 51,
            "start": 25
          },
          "path": "catalog/models.py",
          "symbol": "BookCopy"
        },
        "summary": "BookCopy stores a unique barcode, acquired_on and condition, and holds a CASCADE foreign key to Book with related_name copies; is_on_shelf and current_loan are computed from its loans."
      },
      {
        "contentDigest": "sha256:f75380d7ad97bb61e6cef65408af2fe4385a220a2e322a6df6459d6144bfeb64",
        "id": "ev-loan",
        "kind": "code",
        "locator": {
          "lineRange": {
            "end": 46,
            "start": 8
          },
          "path": "circulation/models.py",
          "symbol": "Loan"
        },
        "summary": "Loan stores a PROTECT foreign key to BookCopy, a CASCADE foreign key to the member, borrowed_at, due_on, a nullable returned_at and a renewals counter."
      },
      {
        "contentDigest": "sha256:ca42bdc5aaada1dac1da94fc8505f7f408073f1106fcdd2d6aa93136acf28244",
        "id": "ev-hold",
        "kind": "code",
        "locator": {
          "lineRange": {
            "end": 59,
            "start": 49
          },
          "path": "circulation/models.py",
          "symbol": "Hold"
        },
        "summary": "Hold stores CASCADE foreign keys to Book and to the member, placed_at and a nullable cancelled_at, and is ordered by placed_at."
      },
      {
        "contentDigest": "sha256:3a32b7b1a3ded2d5cd009fa390989e929c4567f37484bb80c2743a275ea147a1",
        "id": "ev-hold-queue",
        "kind": "code",
        "locator": {
          "lineRange": {
            "end": 71,
            "start": 62
          },
          "path": "circulation/models.py",
          "symbol": "HoldQueue"
        },
        "summary": "HoldQueue is a plain class, not a model: next_for reads the oldest uncancelled Hold for a book, so queue position is computed rather than stored."
      },
      {
        "contentDigest": "sha256:d0b1b7ccbd56d0c9f70629c28e847faa26c119542c42ada9c7c9d0e62bfe3fc6",
        "id": "ev-payment",
        "kind": "code",
        "locator": {
          "lineRange": {
            "end": 24,
            "start": 5
          },
          "path": "fines/models.py",
          "symbol": "FinePayment"
        },
        "summary": "FinePayment stores amount_minor and paid_at, a CASCADE foreign key to the member, a nullable SET_NULL foreign key to the Loan, and a nullable SET_NULL taken_by member."
      },
      {
        "contentDigest": "sha256:0b9b9aae62824ab25943f7c4096b18be1b856ee21506b1a1061f226df6132290",
        "id": "ev-fines-derived",
        "kind": "documentation",
        "locator": {
          "lineRange": {
            "end": 4,
            "start": 1
          },
          "path": "fines/assessment.py"
        },
        "summary": "The assessment module's docstring states that nothing here is stored: a fine is a fact about a loan and a date, not a row."
      },
      {
        "contentDigest": "sha256:1ae28d2e5c8e491843562c8c210f33a0f619a0316cab6279309c97d12fd2fc4c",
        "id": "ev-loan-state-test",
        "kind": "test",
        "locator": {
          "lineRange": {
            "end": 46,
            "start": 45
          },
          "path": "circulation/tests.py",
          "symbol": "LoanStateTests"
        },
        "summary": "The loan-state test class states that a Loan has no status column and that everything follows from its two date fields."
      },
      {
        "contentDigest": "sha256:8775587a63565eee711df7a7c17ff3d122c9da0bce47e1f4217b1eb9915e82ef",
        "id": "ev-cascade-copies-test",
        "kind": "test",
        "locator": {
